        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(amazon-bedrock): add timeouts to model discovery requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Amazon Bedrock model discovery could wait indefinitely when the Bedrock control-plane model listing calls stalled, leaving setup and model catalog refresh paths without a bounded failure.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBedrock discovery now wraps both `ListFoundationModels` and paginated `ListInferenceProfiles` SDK calls in a local 30-second abort deadline using the AWS SDK `client.send(..., { abortSignal })` contract. The existing best-effort fallback remains unchanged: profile discovery failures still degrade to no profiles, and failed foundation discovery still returns an empty discovered catalog.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators get a bounded Bedrock model discovery failure instead of an indefinitely pending setup or catalog refresh when the AWS control plane stalls. Successful discovery behavior and cached catalog behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/amazon-bedrock/discovery.test.ts` passed: 24 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude --model claude-fable-5 --thinking high` reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Verified the installed AWS SDK/Smithy client type accepts `client.send(command, options)` and Smithy HTTP handler options include `abortSignal`.\n\n### 2026-07-12 follow-up: exact-head local discovery timeout proof\n\n- Exact PR head verified locally: `29b7aaff4eb2a5396ab4dd875a2b6e2e14935366`.\n- Command: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/amazon-bedrock/discovery.test.ts`.\n- Result: passed 1 Vitest shard in 19.32s; 24 tests passed.\n- Coverage from the focused file: Bedrock model/profile discovery timeout behavior, abort-aware discovery calls, and fallback completion for stalled discovery paths covered by the PR's local regression tests.\n- This is controlled local provider-path proof only. No live AWS Bedrock API call was made, and no real AWS account, region, network stall, or Bedrock control-plane response was exercised.\n\n",
